%N A399815 Decimal expansion of 4 + 2*sqrt(3) + 4*sqrt(6)/3.
%C A399815 Side length of the smallest equilateral triangle inside which eleven unit circles (radius = 1) can be packed.
%C A399815 See A400358 for the corresponding largest possible minimal pairwise distance of eleven points inside an equilateral triangle with unit side length.
%H A399815 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A399815/b399815.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%H A399815 Hans (J. B. M.) Melissen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2307/2324212">Densest Packings of Congruent Circles in an Equilateral Triangle</a>, The American Mathematical Monthly, Vol. 100, Issue 10 (1993), pp. 916-925 (also available on <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324212">JSTOR</a>).
%H A399815 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_packing_in_an_equilateral_triangle">Circle packing in an equilateral triangle</a>.
%H A399815 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_04">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 4</a>.
%F A399815 Equals 4 + A010469 + 4*A157697.
%F A399815 Equals 2*(A002194 + 1/A400358).
%F A399815 Equals the largest root of 9*x^4 - 144*x^3 + 456*x^2 + 960*x - 4208.
%e A399815 10.7300879388486587179846047826195999231735404818...
%t A399815 First[RealDigits[4 + Sqrt[12] + Sqrt[96]/3, 10, 100]]
